# L §4.4 (tally 2.3, #247; the lead's P19, T's held g13 a7): `overlap_days` is on the list for its two days
# only; a ranged date in its span can turn the count back (0 at both ends, 1 between), so it is the hole naming
# the day; pinned inside the two days 1, outside 0. A ranged first day keeps the list's rule (o_days: its ends
# differ, the hole). Before: `RUN-DOMAIN overlap_days is window(…), not a period`.
=== m.tally
model ov
  tally 2
  on 2026-03-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
source card "invented"
input w: date
input d1: date
input d2: date
version v
  cite card
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  w = window(2026-03-03, 2026-03-20) "c"
  d1 = 2026-03-05 "c"
  d2 = 2026-03-12 "c"
ask o_w: overlap_days(d1, d2, w)
ask o_in: overlap_days(d1, d2, w) with w = 2026-03-10
ask o_out: overlap_days(d1, d2, w) with w = 2026-03-15
ask o_days: overlap_days(w, d2, 2026-03)
=== expect
o_days: ?"date within window(2026-03-03, 2026-03-20) not precise enough for overlap_days" (w)
  unknown day: w
  cut 2026-03-01
o_in: 1
  pinned: w = 2026-03-10
  cut 2026-03-01
o_out: 0
  pinned: w = 2026-03-15
  cut 2026-03-01
o_w: ?"date within window(2026-03-03, 2026-03-20) not precise enough for overlap_days" (w)
  unknown day: w
  cut 2026-03-01
